<h2>10. Current Project Status</h2>
<p><strong>Where exactly does the project stand:</strong> the computational/reference-spectroscopy foundation (DFT + powder Raman) for NAM is essentially complete and manuscript-ready; LPS and LTA reference work is complete but of more modest statistical quality and needs a harmonization pass. The Ag/Si SERS substrate fabrication process is functional and reproducibly enhances the benchmark dye R6G, most recently and strongly on 12&nbsp;August (SNR to 450). However, <strong>zero for three</strong> on the actual diagnostic goal: no biomarker (NAM, LTA, LPS) has been reproducibly detected via SERS on this substrate. NAM has been tried twice (null both times, well-characterized root cause). LTA has been tried once (initially appeared positive, corrected to null via a rigorous artifact check that is now itself one of the project's more valuable methodological contributions). LPS has never been attempted. No experimental work has occurred since 16&nbsp;August.</p>

<h3>Scientific gaps</h3>
<ul>
<li>Whether NAM can be detected on this substrate class at all without capture chemistry &mdash; still open pending the AgNO&#8323; series.</li>
<li>Whether LTA gives any genuine SERS signal on bare Ag &mdash; genuinely untested (14&nbsp;Aug attempt was corrupted by an artifact, not a clean negative).</li>
<li>Whether LPS (best literature precedent of the three) is detectable on this platform at all &mdash; completely open, no data yet.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Experimental gaps</h3>
<ul>
<li>LPS detection experiment (never run).</li>
<li>NAM AgNO&#8323; concentration series (Groups A-D).</li>
<li>LTA repeat under the corrected protocol.</li>
<li>Batch-to-batch substrate reproducibility (only 1 substrate/condition made so far, across all sessions).</li>
</ul>
<h3>Technical gaps</h3>
<ul>
<li>Absolute laser power in mW never measured.</li>
<li>HF stock concentration never recorded/confirmed.</li>
<li>No FESEM/EDS/UV-Vis substrate characterization found anywhere in the reviewed documents, despite being specified in the original Masters-report methodology.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Data gaps</h3>
<ul>
<li>No concentration-response/LOD data for any biomarker on-substrate.</li>
<li>LTA's expanded 136-file fitting branch has unresolved NaN metrics.</li>
<li>No enhancement-factor (EF) calculation exists for the R6G/Ag-Si substrate despite being a stated project KPI (target &gt;10&#8310;).</li>
</ul>
<h3>Validation gaps</h3>
<ul>
<li>Substrate reproducibility (mean correlation 0.7754) remains below the project's own 0.90 target.</li>
<li>No independent-substrate replicate study has ever been run for any condition.</li>
<li>No blank/control/matrix-interference testing has been done for any biomarker in anything beyond pure powder/buffer.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Documentation gaps</h3>
<ul>
<li>NAM DFT method has (at least) two generations (Gaussian 09 vs. 16) still not formally harmonized into one canonical protocol for the thesis/TCS deliverable.</li>
<li>Power units inconsistently reported as % in some branches and W in others.</li>
<li>No live experiment-logging spreadsheet was kept during the 12-14&nbsp;Aug sessions (post-hoc reconstruction was needed) &mdash; a logging convention now exists on paper (Experiment_Plan documents) but has not yet been used in practice.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Integration gaps</h3>
<ul>
<li>No ML/classification layer exists (needs real on-substrate detections first).</li>
<li>No clinical-sample or blood-matrix work has started (biobank SOP exists on paper only, per earlier document review; no evidence of IRB/ethics approval or sample collection in this scope).</li>
<li>No portable/point-of-care hardware integration has begun.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Dependency ranking</strong> (as implied by the documents' own staged plans, not an external scoring):</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Must be completed first:</strong> LPS detection attempt (highest chance of a first real positive, unblocks confidence in the whole platform); resolving the absolute laser-power-in-mW gap (needed to interpret every other measurement correctly).</li>
<li><strong>Can be done in parallel:</strong> NAM AgNO&#8323; series and LTA repeat &mdash; independent of each other and of LPS, though instrument/fume-hood time is shared.</li>
<li><strong>Depends on previous results:</strong> NAM concentration series (only after AgNO&#8323; series analyzed); MPBA functionalization (only after bare-Ag NAM route is exhausted); cysteamine-SAM for LTA (only if bare-Ag LTA fails); cross-analyte comparison and LOD/LOQ work (only after at least one clean positive detection).</li>
<li><strong>Final-stage work:</strong> ML classification, clinical/blood-matrix testing, POC hardware integration, manuscript submissions beyond the NAM reference paper.</li>
</ol>

<h2>11. Remaining Technical/Scientific Gaps</h2>
<p>(Consolidated from Section 10 above &mdash; repeated here per the requested structure.) The single largest unresolved question is whether any of the three biomarkers can be detected label-free on the current bare-Ag/black-Si platform at all; LPS is the best-positioned to answer this first given its unique published precedent. The second-largest gap is basic substrate/instrument characterization that every other document keeps flagging but nothing has yet resolved: absolute laser power in mW, HF stock concentration, and FESEM/EDS/UV-Vis substrate characterization.</p>

