<h3>Phase 3 &mdash; Validation</h3>
<ul>
<li>Repeatability: &ge;3 spots per condition, minimum, per protocol already defined.</li>
<li>Reproducibility: independent-substrate replicates &mdash; not yet done for any condition; should be added to every future experiment (2nd substrate per condition minimum).</li>
<li>Controls: same-session blank before every analyte measurement (a real gap in earlier sessions, now fixed in the written protocols).</li>
<li>Specificity: bare unetched-Si negative control for LPS (already specified); GlcNAc/glucose selectivity testing deferred until NAM shows any bare-Ag signal.</li>
<li>Concentration dependence: dilution series specified for all three biomarkers; not yet executed for any.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Phase 4 &mdash; Data analysis</h3>
<ul>
<li>Preprocessing: despike (mandatory, new) &rarr; ALS baseline &rarr; Savitzky-Golay smoothing &rarr; normalize &mdash; consistent with the mature pipeline already used for NAM reference data.</li>
<li>Peak detection: SNR&ge;3, &ge;3-pixel width, &plusmn;5&nbsp;cm&#8315;&sup1; tolerance &mdash; now standard across all three biomarker protocols.</li>
<li>Statistical analysis: currently strong for DFT-vs-experiment (MAE/RMSE/Pearson); needs extending to dose-response/LOD statistics once any positive detection exists.</li>
<li>Classification: not yet appropriate &mdash; no real training data exists.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Phase 5 &mdash; Final prototype/project deliverable</h3>
<p>Not yet definable in concrete engineering terms from the available documents &mdash; this is explicitly one of the items to confirm with Prof. Ajay today (see Section 20), since the TCS deliverable scope (hardware? software? sensing chemistry only?) has not been stated in any document reviewed.</p>

