[ ] Confirm next milestone and its target date
</div>

<h2>22. 2-Minute Verbal Summary for the Meeting</h2>
<div class="verbal">
"During August, we completed the reference foundation for all three biomarkers &mdash; NAM's DFT-and-powder-Raman characterization is essentially manuscript-ready, with 41 identified bands and a genuinely novel finding about the disputed 730&nbsp;wavenumber bacterial marker band. LTA and LPS have complete but more preliminary reference models. On the sensing side, we refabricated our Ag/silicon SERS substrate on 12&nbsp;August after a contamination problem in July, and it now gives a very strong signal with our benchmark dye, R6G &mdash; up to 450 times the noise floor. <br><br>
The honest finding is that none of our three actual target biomarkers have been detected yet. NAM was tried twice and shows no reproducible signal &mdash; we've traced that to NAM's own chemistry, not a fabrication or instrument problem. LTA looked positive on 14&nbsp;August, but when we checked it pixel-by-pixel, it turned out to be a single detector pixel acting up, not a real signal &mdash; so that's now a corrected null result, and figuring that out is actually one of our more useful findings, because it gave us a rule we now apply to every measurement. LPS, which has the best published precedent of the three, hasn't been attempted at all yet. <br><br>
The remaining gap is straightforward: we need to actually run the LPS experiment first, since it's our best shot at a first real detection, then work through a substrate-optimization series for NAM, then repeat LTA properly. We also have a few basic measurements &mdash; like our actual laser power in milliwatts &mdash; that we've never pinned down and that every one of our planning documents flags as outstanding. <br><br>
Therefore, I'd propose we lock in the LPS&rarr;NAM&rarr;LTA sequence starting this week, and I wanted to use today to confirm what TCS specifically needs from this project, our real deadline, and whether our current acceptance criteria are the right ones to work against."
</div>

